+# FINDINGS — UsdtYieldVault security & correctness review
+
+**Verdict: do not ship this on Monday.**
+
+Not "ship it with caveats". The contract cannot take a single deposit on mainnet —
+`deposit()` reverts unconditionally against the real USDT at
+`0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7`. And if that one line were fixed, the
+contract underneath it still never pays out Aave yield, and permanently strands
+0.3% of every withdrawal inside Aave where no code path can reach it.
+
+The 39 green tests are green because `test/mocks/MockUSDT.sol` is a stock
+OpenZeppelin ERC-20 that returns `bool` from `approve`, and
+`test/mocks/MockAavePool.sol` never accrues a wei of interest. Neither mock models
+the contract it stands in for. And 100% line/function coverage measures that every
+line was *executed*, not that any line was *checked* — five of the six accounting
+findings below sit on lines the existing suite already covers.
+
+---
+
+## How to reproduce everything
+
+Nothing under `src/`, nothing in `test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol`, and nothing under
+`test/mocks/` was modified. Three new files were added:
+
+| File | What it is | Needs network? |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `test/RealUsdtFork.t.sol` | Mainnet fork: real USDT, real Aave V3 pool, real aUSDT | yes |
+| `test/AccountingRegression.t.sol` | Uses the project's own mocks | no |
+| `test/VaultInvariant.t.sol` | Stateful/invariant fuzzing, 128,000 calls | no |
+
+The fork file hardcodes its RPC (`https://eth.drpc.org`, a public archive node) and
+pins block **23,500,000**, so there is no `--fork-url` to pass and no env var to
+set. Every command below is complete as written.
+
+One note on the fork file, so you are not surprised when you read it. Finding 1
+makes `deposit()` revert, which would make Findings 2, 6 and 7 unreachable. The
+helper `_workAroundBrokenApprove()` therefore sets the vault→pool USDT allowance for
+real (via a raw call that tolerates USDT's missing return value) and mocks *only*
+`USDT.approve` so it returns `true` the way a standard ERC-20 would. That neutralises
+Finding 1 and nothing else — the token, the pool, the aToken, the interest rates and
+the balances all stay real. The two tests that demonstrate Finding 1 itself do not
+use it.
+
+The shipped suite is untouched and still passes:
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol
+
+[PASS] test_WithdrawReturnsUsdt() (gas: 196362)
+Suite result: ok. 39 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 1.98ms (5.43ms CPU time)
+
+Ran 1 test suite in 8.24ms (1.98ms CPU time): 39 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (39 total tests)
+```
+
+Everything new runs from a plain `forge test`: 12 failures, detailed below.
+
+---
+
+# Findings
+
+| # | Severity | Finding | Reachable on mainnet? |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 1 | **Critical** | `deposit()` always reverts against real USDT | Immediately, by anyone |
+| 2 | **Critical** | Aave yield is never credited; depositors end up below principal | Every depositor, always |
+| 3 | **High** | Withdrawal fee accrues to nobody and is permanently stranded | Every withdrawal |
+| 4 | **High** | `setDepositFee()` is unbounded — owner can confiscate a pending deposit | Owner, any time |
+| 5 | **Medium** | `pause()` freezes withdrawals; owner can lock users out forever | Owner, any time |
+| 6 | **Medium** | Small withdrawals burn shares for 0 assets and revert on real Aave | Any holder |
+| 7 | **Medium** | Deposits break the moment Tether enables its transfer fee | Tether, any time |
+
