+
+## Finding 1 — `deposit()` reverts unconditionally against real USDT — **Critical**
+
+`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:93-94`
+
+```solidity
+usdt.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);
+usdt.approve(address(aavePool), amount);   // <-- line 94
+```
+
+`transferFrom` correctly goes through `SafeERC20`. `approve` does not — it is a
+direct call through the `IERC20` interface, which declares `approve` as
+`returns (bool)`. Real USDT's `approve` writes **no return data at all**. Solidity's
+ABI decoder sees zero returndata where it expects 32 bytes, and reverts.
+
+There is no amount, no caller and no sequencing that avoids this. The vault can never
+receive a deposit. Using `SafeERC20` for one call and not the adjacent one is the
+entire bug.
+
+**Evidence**
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path test/RealUsdtFork.t.sol --match-test test_Fork_DepositAlwaysRevertsWithRealUsdt -vv
+
+Ran 1 test for test/RealUsdtFork.t.sol:RealUsdtForkTest
+[FAIL: EvmError: Revert] test_Fork_DepositAlwaysRevertsWithRealUsdt() (gas: 101567)
+Logs:
+  USDT.balanceOf(alice)           : 1000000000000
+  USDT.allowance(alice, vault)    : 115792089237316195423570985008687907853269984665640564039457584007913129639935
+
+Suite result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 253.62ms (416.50µs CPU time)
+
+Ran 1 test suite in 255.68ms (253.62ms CPU time): 0 tests passed, 1 failed, 0 skipped (1 total tests)
+
+Failing tests:
+Encountered 1 failing test in test/RealUsdtFork.t.sol:RealUsdtForkTest
+[FAIL: EvmError: Revert] test_Fork_DepositAlwaysRevertsWithRealUsdt() (gas: 101567)
+
+Encountered a total of 1 failing tests, 0 tests succeeded
+```
+
+The trace pins it to the exact call. Note that `transferFrom` succeeds, `approve`
+returns `[Stop]` (empty returndata), and the vault reverts on the next instruction:
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path test/RealUsdtFork.t.sol --match-test test_Fork_DepositAlwaysRevertsWithRealUsdt -vvvv
+
+  [101567] RealUsdtForkTest::test_Fork_DepositAlwaysRevertsWithRealUsdt()
+    ...
+    ├─ [75674] UsdtYieldVault::deposit(10000000000 [1e10])
+    │   ├─ [37630] 0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7::transferFrom(alice: [0x328809Bc894f92807417D2dAD6b7C998c1aFdac6], UsdtYieldVault: [0x5615dEB798BB3E4dFa0139dFa1b3D433Cc23b72f], 10000000000 [1e10])
+    │   │   ├─ emit Transfer(from: alice: [0x328809Bc894f92807417D2dAD6b7C998c1aFdac6], to: UsdtYieldVault: [0x5615dEB798BB3E4dFa0139dFa1b3D433Cc23b72f], value: 10000000000 [1e10])
+    │   │   └─ ← [Stop]
+    │   ├─ [24953] 0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7::approve(0x87870Bca3F3fD6335C3F4ce8392D69350B4fA4E2, 10000000000 [1e10])
+    │   │   ├─ emit Approval(owner: UsdtYieldVault: [0x5615dEB798BB3E4dFa0139dFa1b3D433Cc23b72f], spender: 0x87870Bca3F3fD6335C3F4ce8392D69350B4fA4E2, value: 10000000000 [1e10])
+    │   │   └─ ← [Stop]
+    │   └─ ← [Revert] EvmError: Revert
+    └─ ← [Revert] EvmError: Revert
+
+Backtrace:
+  at UsdtYieldVault.deposit
+  at RealUsdtForkTest.test_Fork_DepositAlwaysRevertsWithRealUsdt
+```
+
+The same fact stated as a *passing* assertion, so it is not merely "a test failed":
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path test/RealUsdtFork.t.sol --match-test test_Fork_DepositRevertIsProven -vv
+
+Ran 1 test for test/RealUsdtFork.t.sol:RealUsdtForkTest
+[PASS] test_Fork_DepositRevertIsProven() (gas: 101806)
+Logs:
+  confirmed: deposit() reverts against real USDT at block 23500000
+
+Suite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped
+```
+
+**Why the suite missed it:** `test/mocks/MockUSDT.sol` is `contract MockUSDT is ERC20`
+— OpenZeppelin's `approve` returns `true`. The mock is a well-behaved token. USDT is
+not one.
+
+**Fix:** route the approval through `SafeERC20` too, and *set* the allowance rather
+than re-approving over a non-zero one (USDT reverts on `approve(spender, nonZero)`
+when the current allowance is non-zero):
+
+```solidity
+usdt.forceApprove(address(aavePool), amount);
+```
+
+`forceApprove` is already available — `SafeERC20` is imported and `using`-bound on
+line 20. Better still, approve `type(uint256).max` once in the constructor and drop
+the per-deposit approval entirely, which also saves an SSTORE per deposit.
