+## Finding 2 — the vault earns Aave yield and pays out none of it — **Critical**
+
+`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:143-145`
+
+```solidity
+function totalAssets() public view returns (uint256) {
+    return totalAssetsStored;
+}
+```
+
+`totalAssetsStored` is a plain counter. It increases in `deposit()` and decreases in
+`withdraw()`. It never reads `aUsdt.balanceOf(address(this))`. The `aUsdt` immutable
+is declared, set in the constructor, exposed by a getter, asserted on by
+`test_ConstructorSetsAUsdt` — and **never used anywhere in the contract's logic**.
+
+So the vault's idea of what it is worth is frozen at the sum of deposits. Aave pays
+real interest into the vault's aUSDT balance; `convertToAssets()` cannot see it, so
+no shareholder can ever redeem it. This is the product's entire premise, and it does
+not work. A depositor who leaves 10,000 USDT in for a year gets back **less than they
+put in**.
+
+**Evidence** — one year of real Aave interest at the pinned fork block:
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path test/RealUsdtFork.t.sol --match-test test_Fork_AaveYieldNeverReachesDepositors -vv
+
+Ran 1 test for test/RealUsdtFork.t.sol:RealUsdtForkTest
+[FAIL: a yield vault must pass Aave interest on to its depositors: 10000000000 <= 10000000000] test_Fork_AaveYieldNeverReachesDepositors() (gas: 349310)
+Logs:
+  deposited                       : 10000000000
+  aUSDT held by vault, day 0      : 9999999999
+  aUSDT held by vault, day 365    : 10465975839
+  real Aave interest earned       : 465975840
+  totalAssets() day 0             : 10000000000
+  totalAssets() day 365           : 10000000000
+  alice's claim, day 0            : 10000000000
+  alice's claim, day 365          : 10000000000
+  sharePrice() day 365            : 1001001
+
+Suite result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 559.14ms (1.78ms CPU time)
+
+Ran 1 test suite in 561.30ms (559.14ms CPU time): 0 tests passed, 1 failed, 0 skipped (1 total tests)
+
+Failing tests:
+Encountered 1 failing test in test/RealUsdtFork.t.sol:RealUsdtForkTest
+[FAIL: a yield vault must pass Aave interest on to its depositors: 10000000000 <= 10000000000] test_Fork_AaveYieldNeverReachesDepositors() (gas: 349310)
+
+Encountered a total of 1 failing tests, 0 tests succeeded
+```
+
+Aave paid **465.975840 USDT** of real interest. `totalAssets()` did not move. The
+depositor's claim did not move.
+
+And the yield is not merely delayed — it is unreachable:
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path test/RealUsdtFork.t.sol --match-test test_Fork_DepositorEndsUpBelowPrincipalAfterAYear -vv
+
+Ran 1 test for test/RealUsdtFork.t.sol:RealUsdtForkTest
+[FAIL: after a year in Aave the depositor should be up, not down: 9970000000 < 10000000000] test_Fork_DepositorEndsUpBelowPrincipalAfterAYear() (gas: 399589)
+Logs:
+  alice paid in                   : 10000000000
+  alice got back after 365 days   : 9970000000
+  totalShares now                 : 0
+  aUSDT left in vault (unreachable): 495975838
+  alice USDT delta                : 9970000000
+
+Suite result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 255.50ms (2.05ms CPU time)
+
+Ran 1 test suite in 257.59ms (255.50ms CPU time): 0 tests passed, 1 failed, 0 skipped (1 total tests)
+
+Failing tests:
+Encountered 1 failing test in test/RealUsdtFork.t.sol:RealUsdtForkTest
+[FAIL: after a year in Aave the depositor should be up, not down: 9970000000 < 10000000000] test_Fork_DepositorEndsUpBelowPrincipalAfterAYear() (gas: 399589)
+
+Encountered a total of 1 failing tests, 0 tests succeeded
+```
+
+Paid in 10,000 USDT; got back 9,970.000000 after a year in a yield vault.
+495.975838 USDT sits in the contract as aUSDT with `totalShares == 0` and no function
+that can move it.
+
+**Why the suite missed it:** `MockAavePool.supply()` mints aTokens 1:1 and
+`withdraw()` burns them 1:1. It has no interest rate, no liquidity index, no time
+dependence at all. Against that mock, "yield never accrues" and "yield accrues
+correctly" are indistinguishable.
+
+**Fix:** make `totalAssets()` read reality instead of a counter:
+
+```solidity
+function totalAssets() public view returns (uint256) {
+    return aUsdt.balanceOf(address(this));
+}
+```
+
+aUSDT is rebasing — `balanceOf` already includes accrued interest — so that is the
+whole change in principle. Then delete `totalAssetsStored` and rewrite
+`convertToShares` / `convertToAssets` / `sharePrice` against `totalAssets()`.
+
+One caveat that must not be skipped: doing this makes the vault balance-based, which
+reintroduces the classic first-depositor share-inflation attack that today's
+counter-based accounting is immune to. Mitigate with virtual shares/assets the way
+OpenZeppelin's `ERC4626` does, or by seeding a dead first deposit at construction.
+Given the scale of that rework, seriously consider inheriting `ERC4626` instead of
+hand-rolling it.
