+
+`totalShares == 0`, `totalAssetsStored == 0`, and **5.999999 USDT** of aUSDT is
+locked in the contract with no code path to it.
+
+This is not a dust problem. It is 30 bps of every withdrawal, forever. Stateful
+fuzzing over 128,000 random deposit/withdraw calls:
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path test/VaultInvariant.t.sol
+
+[FAIL: vault holds aUSDT that no share can ever redeem: 181481677069 != 181431338133]
+	[Sequence] (original: 7, shrunk: 2)
+		sender=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000127 addr=[test/VaultInvariant.t.sol:VaultHandler]0x5991A2dF15A8F6A256D3Ec51E99254Cd3fb576A9 calldata=deposit(uint256,uint256) args=[6, 533]
+		sender=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001409 addr=[test/VaultInvariant.t.sol:VaultHandler]0x5991A2dF15A8F6A256D3Ec51E99254Cd3fb576A9 calldata=withdraw(uint256,uint256) args=[226666820370829094906336830641633794498 [2.266e38], 2513521144989350421441909012131896138 [2.513e36]]
+ invariant_EveryAssetHeldIsClaimableBySomeone() (runs: 0, calls: 0, reverts: 0)
+```
+
+It breaks in **two calls** — one deposit, one withdrawal. (The shrunk sequence is
+fuzzer-chosen, so your counterexample numbers will differ; the failure will not.)
+The call summary over a full run:
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path test/VaultInvariant.t.sol --match-test invariant_CallSummary -vv
+
+[PASS] invariant_CallSummary() (runs: 256, calls: 128000, reverts: 0)
+Logs:
+  deposit calls                   : 264
+  withdraw calls                  : 227
+  total USDT deposited            : 14404017177257
+  total USDT withdrawn            : 13700576797425
+  aUSDT held by vault             : 703440379832
+  totalAssetsStored (claimable)   : 662214973277
+  UNCLAIMABLE, stuck forever      : 41225406555
+```
+
+14.4M USDT of deposit flow produced **41,225 USDT** that nobody can ever withdraw.
+
+**Fix:** decide which behaviour you actually want, and make the code say it.
+
+- To match the docs (fee accrues to remaining holders): subtract only what actually
+  leaves the vault — `totalAssetsStored -= netAssets;`. The fee then stays inside the
+  shareholders' claim and marks up the share price, exactly as advertised.
+- To pay the fee to a treasury: keep `-= grossAssets` and add a second
+  `aavePool.withdraw(address(usdt), fee, feeRecipient)`.
+
+Either way, wire the invariant from `test/VaultInvariant.t.sol`
+(`aUsdt.balanceOf(vault) == totalAssets()`) into CI. It is the property that catches
+this whole class of bug. Note that Finding 2's fix makes this one disappear as a side
+effect, since a balance-based `totalAssets()` cannot drift from the balance.
